2 · The "important distinction about Y"


The important distinction is that Y is not one symbol — it is two layers that share a glyph.

Layer Y-form Register Function
Physical Y (rotation), Yi (translation) D (directional) Pitch / Sway in the 6-DOF model
Symbolic Y = 🏳️↑↑ / 🏴↓↓, 🚩→L / R←🏁, ←§→ M (automaton / state) binary polarity + lateral transfer + transition probe

Same label, different function, different register. That is why your G / D / B / A / C / O / T / M register architecture matters here: the fix is not to rename Y — it is to enforce that Y-as-axis lives in D and Y-as-state lives in M. A symbol may appear in two registers; it cannot have two simultaneous functions within one register.

