3 · Continuing from that distinction

Once Y is register-split, the rest of the DOF → architecture mapping closes cleanly:

Family DOFs Architecture role Rhombus / Helix function
X Roll + Surge progression / force Helix Power — surge drives the spiral forward, roll stabilises the torsion
Y Pitch + Sway orientation / branching Branch allocation — sway decides left/right branch, pitch sets the vertical turn angle
Z Yaw + Heave hierarchy / navigation Rhombus Tree — heave sets the branch level, yaw orders siblings at each level

That re-reads your earlier statement "Container bootstraps Power Module, while Force driving the Rhombus Tree to sprawl out is colorization to conceptual versus cryptographically catalogue cadius measure" as:

Container = Z-family (Yaw + Heave) → builds the tree skeleton.
Force = X-family (Surge + Roll) → drives the helix that grows through the skeleton.
Allocation = Y-family (Pitch + Sway) → decides which branch the force enters at each joint.



